\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Temporal window length ablation ($W \in \{1, 3, 5, 7\}$) for the moving average filter on the validation split, showing $F_1$-score ($\uparrow $) and False Alerts/min ($\downarrow $) across window spans (42~ms to 292~ms at 24~Hz). $W = 5$ achieves the best trade-off on validation sequences, cutting false alerts by 63\% with modest added delay.}}{4}{}\protected@file@percent }
